description:
Aypa Power is a leading developer, owner, and operator of utility-scale energy storage and hybrid renewable projects that power our communities and cities. Our mission is to responsibly decarbonize the grid and make North American energy markets more affordable, sustainable, and efficient. Aypa is well-capitalized and uniquely positioned to lean forward on projects with well-suited deal structures to meet our customers' needs. We have been at the forefront of energy storage development since our first energy storage project came online in 2018. As a leader in our industry, we have over 22 GW of utility-scale energy storage and hybrid renewable energy projects in development and 33 projects in operation or construction across North America.

As a Transmission Interconnection Manager, you will oversee the interconnection of new power generation projects to the grid. This role involves managing the interconnection process, ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements, coordinating with utilities and transmission operators, and supporting project development teams. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in electrical engineering (power systems), project management, and knowledge of grid interconnection Tariffs.

**Responsibilities:**

* Create and manage interconnection applications from inception to COD;
* Track and deliver on project milestones and other associated requirements;
* Perform system modeling and transmission analysis for a growing portfolio of Energy Storage, Solar, Wind, and Hybrid projects;
* Replicate ISO and utility interconnection studies to identify potential impacts and costs of interconnecting generation to power systems;
* Act as a subject matter expert on interconnection queues, transmission plans, Tariff, and business practice changes;
* Provide Transmission & Interconnection due diligence support for ongoing M&A;
* Collaborate with teammates supporting project development, market analysis, and market forecasting;
* Prepare summa
